{"judgements":[{"id":"T1","kind":"answered","quotes":["An accepted import drops the uploaded file of every owner session (M11); a confirmation shown in another session is refused because the import is closed (rule 8).","When the closure exists, uploading, showing the mapping or the import's confirmation step and confirming are refused, and a sign-out goes on.","Stage (1) comes first — the session, the CSRF value and the confirmation value, used up when it was carried (A13 rule 6) — and this refusal comes before every other of the import's own checks."],"later_state":null,"precedent":null,"divergence":"","why":"An accepted import drops every session's upload and the closure prevents every further import step, while a same-session resubmission is first refused because its one-time confirmation value was consumed.","witness":{"initial":"","events":[],"outcomes":["",""],"observer":"","basis":[]},"bases":[]},{"id":"T2","kind":"answered","quotes":["`module:owner_interface` renders the sign-in form and every page, sets and reads the session cookie and carries the CSRF value in every form; it decides nothing (A13 rules 1, 5, 7).","The sign-in form posts the credential;
